From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: encode the visible size on gen1

A 1920x1080 encode on SM8250 comes out 1920x1088, with no cropping in
the SPS, so a client shows eight rows of junk at the bottom. Setting the
crop with VIDIOC_S_SELECTION makes no difference.

Gen1 sends HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_FRAME_SIZE from fmt_src and fmt_dst, which
are aligned to 32 and 16. Venus drives the same HFI and sends the
visible size on both ports instead; the aligned layout already goes to
the firmware in UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_INFO, and the firmware writes
the frame cropping into the SPS. Gen2 gets the same result from
HFI_PROP_CROP_OFFSETS.

Send the crop rectangle (no larger than the raw size) on the input port
and the unaligned scaled size on the output port. The decoder is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 2e249c5..fb7434b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -794,12 +794,42 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_session_set_property(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 packet
 	return hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, packet_type, payload, payload_size);
 }
 
+/*
+ * As venus does: the visible size goes to the firmware on both ports, the
+ * aligned buffer layout goes in UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_INFO, and the
+ * firmware crops the bitstream to the visible size. Sending the aligned
+ * CAPTURE size instead made a 1080p stream 1088 lines tall.
+ */
+static int iris_hfi_gen1_set_enc_resolution(struct iris_inst *inst)
+{
+	u32 ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_FRAME_SIZE;
+	struct hfi_framesize fs;
+	int ret;
+
+	fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_INPUT;
+	fs.width = min(inst->crop.width, inst->enc_raw_width);
+	fs.height = min(inst->crop.height, inst->enc_raw_height);
+
+	ret = hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, ptype, &fs, sizeof(fs));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_OUTPUT;
+	fs.width = inst->enc_scale_width;
+	fs.height = inst->enc_scale_height;
+
+	return hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, ptype, &fs, sizeof(fs));
+}
+
 static int iris_hfi_gen1_set_resolution(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 {
 	u32 ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_FRAME_SIZE;
 	struct hfi_framesize fs;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (inst->domain == ENCODER)
+		return iris_hfi_gen1_set_enc_resolution(inst);
+
 	if (!iris_drc_pending(inst) && !(inst->sub_state & IRIS_INST_SUB_FIRST_IPSC)) {
 		fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_INPUT;
 		fs.width = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.width;
